erged from  upon re-entering one room to investigate  the d-class was ordered to take a  surgical knife back to command for  further study however as soon as he  lifted the knife communication  immediately cut off and the foundation  was unable to re-establish contact a  third test was held shortly after to  determine what happened to the d-class  as well as explore the second floor of  scp-1098  this time using another remote  controlled drone the drone found that  the house on its second floor had a  sewing workshop filled with all the  materials you would expect to find in  such including threads machinery and  tools multiple corpses were found all  dressed in 18th century clothes their  eyes replaced with artificial ones and  with strings sewn into their bodies upon  the drone's return communication was cut  off yet again and when the hour period  was up and the house's door opened there  was no sign of it anywhere the fourth  test into scp-1098 involved another  d-class personnel who was instructed to  attempt to leave the building before an  hour passed after entering the d-class  reported a throbbing headache and  immediate pressure in his ears he  reported that someone was crying in the  farthest room on the first floor but the  equipment couldn't pick anything up  after entering he reported that he saw a  little girl wearing an old-fashioned  dress and she was dancing and crying  being pulled upward into motion by the  strings that were sewn onto her back  these strings on camera were completely  invisible to the foundation leading the  command to believe that the d-class was  experiencing hallucinations the d-class  simply stood and observed almost  transfixed by the girl he remarked that  it seemed like the string stretched on  forever and that there was no ceiling  even though the foundation could clearly  see the ceiling of the room on the  camera after five minutes of silence and  observation a startling clap was heard  as the camera's visuals cut out 